    [BugFix][Perf] Fix MoE MulsAdd fusion matching and preserve intermediate rounding (#19778)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Extend MulsAdd fusion to cover both operand orders of ordinary addition
    and single-element `torch._foreach_add`. The existing pattern only
    matches `x * scale + y`, missing the shared-first `foreach_add`
    used by the current Ascend MoE output combine.
    
    Keep raw in-place multiplications and patterns with additional consumers
    unfused to preserve mutation and data dependencies. The Triton kernel
    arithmetic remains unchanged.
    
    Co-authored-by: 2luckydog <2981945956@qq.com>
    Co-authored-by: liuwj-research <liuwj.2008@tsinghua.org.cn>
    Co-authored-by: westbook1006 <1210973614@qq.com>
    Co-authored-by: zmc1997 <742133686@qq.com>
    Signed-off-by: mengguangxin <mgx0018@163.com>
    
    ### Does this PR introduce any user-facing change?
    
    No new APIs or configuration options. The existing `fuse_muls_add`
    option now covers additional MoE multiply/add patterns on supported
    hardware.
    
    Profiling confirmed that the tested main-model MoE path executes
    `muls_add_kernel`. End-to-end ITL benefits remain to be validated.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Validated the fusion patterns in a real GLM-5.2 W8A8C8 1P1D
    deployment; model accuracy remained normal.
    - NPU profiling showed 1,875 fused kernel calls per TP rank, matching 25
    main-model forwards × 75 MoE layers; the corresponding standalone Muls
    and ForeachAdd calls disappeared.
    - Passed 18 isolated CPU checks covering both addition forms, both
    operand orders, supported dtypes, and cases that must remain unfused.
    - Passed Ruff lint and formatting, Python syntax, Markdown lint, and
    `git diff --check`.
    
